item.description:
Combined activity feed for managers/HR/admins: attendance correction/regularization + leave only (reimbursements excluded; use /api/reimbursements/requests). Sorted by created_at (latest first). For manager logins, data is restricted to employees in departments managed by that manager.

Optional status filter: status=PENDING|APPROVED|REJECTED|CANCELLED (case-insensitive) applies to both ATTENDANCE and LEAVE overall status. Omit for all statuses.

Response shape:
{
  "page": 1,
  "limit": 10,
  "total": 42,
  "total_pages": 5,
  "data": [
    {
      "type": "ATTENDANCE" | "LEAVE",
      "id": "...",            // original request id
      "employee": {
        "id": "...",
        "employee_id": "EMP-001",
        "full_name": "Sarah Jenkins",
        "role": "employee",
        "designation": "Senior UX Designer",
        "profile_image_url": "https://..." or null
      },
      "status": "PENDING" | "APPROVED" | "REJECTED" | "CANCELLED",
      "created_at": "...",
      "summary": "Reason text",
      "details": {
        // For ATTENDANCE: request_date, wrong_punch_type, corrected_time
        // For LEAVE: start_date, end_date, leave_type_name
      }
    },
    ...
  ]
}

Use this endpoint to drive a unified approvals/activity view; for full details, the UI can still call the existing per-type detail APIs.

Date range filtering: when from_date and to_date are provided, ATTENDANCE entries are filtered by request_date and LEAVE entries are included when leave duration overlaps the inclusive range.

request.description:
Single composite endpoint that returns a user's profile overview, segmented into about, work, documents, and payroll sections.

Auth:
- Allowed roles: admin, hr, manager, employee
- Admin/HR can fetch any user in the same org using userId.
- Manager/Employee can only fetch their own profile (userId must match their id).

Response shape:
{
  "message": "Employee overview retrieved successfully",
  "data": {
    "about": { /* personal + contact info; includes profile_image_url */ },
    "work": { /* job details, reporting manager, team, work location */ },
    "documents": { /* recent documents list */ },
    "payroll": {
      "uan_number": "123456789012" or null,
      "pf_number": "PF123456" or null
    }
  }
}

`payroll` values come from `user_payroll_details` for the target user.

Get bank, asset, and payroll identifier details for a specific employee (admin/hr/manager).

Response shape:
```json
{
  "message": "Bank and asset details retrieved successfully",
  "data": {
    "bank_details": {
      "user_id": "...",
      "ifsc_code": "HDFC0001234",
      "bank_name": "HDFC Bank",
      "account_number": "50100456789012",
      "account_holder_name": "Fathima Mary J",
      "bank_proof_url": "https://...",
      "bank_proof_key": "orgs/.../finance/bank_proof_...",
      "created_at": "2026-04-09T10:35:32.680Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-04-09T10:35:32.680Z"
    },
    "asset_details": {
      "asset_device_pref": "MACBOOK",
      "asset_agreement_accepted": true,
      "device_serial_number": "C02XXX123ABC"
    },
    "payroll_details": {
      "uan_number": "123456789012",
      "pf_number": "PF123456"
    }
  }
}
```

Notes:
- `bank_details` is null if no bank record exists.
- `bank_details.bank_proof_url` and `bank_details.bank_proof_key` store the cancelled cheque upload.
- `payroll_details.uan_number` and `payroll_details.pf_number` are sourced from `user_payroll_details` and may be null.

